{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 94.7% similarity to AP971: Phylloseptin-H12. It differs from AP971 only by one residue N17 in this peptide and D in AP971. Structure: Helical in 50% TFE. Activity: Active against S. aureus or MRSA NCTC 12497 (MIC 32.97 uM), MBEC =33 uM, E.faecalis NCTC 12697 (MIC 263.78 uM), E.coli NCTC 10418 (MIC >263.78 uM), and C.albicans NCYC 1467 (MIC 131.89 uM). In vitro Toxicity: 50% hemo.lytic concentration (HC50) 109 uM. anticancer effect: LD50 (MTT assays) 28.48-37.96 uM to cancer cells MB435s, H157, PC-3, U251MG, HCT116, and MCF-7 ( Liu et al., 2019). Updated 8/2020", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "28850103", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2017 Aug 29;22(9). pii: E1428. doi: 10.3390/molecules22091428. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03057", "source_id": "AP03057", "source_numeric_id": "03057", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03057", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Phylloseptins that Defense against Gram-Positive Bacteria and Inhibit the Proliferation of the Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer Cell Line, from the Skin Secretions of Phyllomedusa Frogs", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Hemolytic, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (94.7%) to Phylloseptin-PC, differing only at residue 10 (G10 here vs. T10). Activity: Active against S. aureus NCTC 10788 (MIC 4.14 uM), MRSA NCTC 10788 (4.14 uM), E. faecalis NCTC 12697 (MIC 16.56 uM), E. coli NCTC 10418 (MIC 16.56 uM), C. albicans NCYC 1467 (MIC 2.07 uM). Antibiofilm against S. aureus MBEC = 4 uM. Structure: Helical in 50% TFE. In vitro Toxicity: 50% hemolytic concentration (HC50) 22.8 uM, highly hemolytic. Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "28850103", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Molecules. 2017 Aug 29;22(9):1428. doi: 10.3390/molecules22091428. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03239", "source_id": "AP03239", "source_numeric_id": "03239", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03239", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Phylloseptins that Defense against Gram-Positive Bacteria and Inhibit the Proliferation of the Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer Cell Line, from the Skin Secretions of Phyllomedusa Frogs", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
